<div id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GUI+CLI hybrid agents have become an active direction in computer-use research <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2026</a>)</cite>, including our previous work, Qwen-UI-Agent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., 2026</a>)</cite>. As discussed in Section <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 Definition ‣ 2 Generalist CUA: Definition and Positioning ‣ OpenGCUA: Toward a Fully Open Stack for Generalist Computer Use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, the batched GUI+CLI formulation is a special case of GCUA. We compare this baseline with the full OpenGCUA setting. Both provide GUI and CLI access, but OpenGCUA introduces code execution and model-initiated workflow control, letting the model decide what to observe, how to act, and how to organize its work.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OpenGCUA achieves higher task scores with fewer reported steps.</span>
In the selected runs, OpenGCUA increases task scores by <span id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.4 to 9.1 points</span> across all four models, with lower reported steps per task (Table <a href="#S3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 3.3.3 GUI+CLI Hybrid CUA versus GCUA ‣ 3.3 Experiments on Agent Design ‣ 3 Agent Design: Code Execution and Harness-to-Model Decision Transfer ‣ OpenGCUA: Toward a Fully Open Stack for Generalist Computer Use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). Qwen3.8-Max improves from 57.2 to 64.0 with <span id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">13.8% fewer steps</span>, while GLM-5.3-Flash improves from 55.8 to 64.9 with <span id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7.6% fewer steps</span>. These results suggest that effective hybrid computer use depends not only on interface access, but also on control over execution and workflow. Code execution lets intermediate results determine subsequent GUI and shell operations within a single program. Harness-to-model decision transfer extends the model’s control to when visual feedback is requested and how task progress is recorded. The comparison evaluates these mechanisms jointly.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.3.4 </span>Code-Execution Ablation</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Code execution improves task scores and reduces interaction steps.</span>
We compare four execution configurations for Qwen3.8-Max, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, and GLM-5.3-Flash: single-action GUI execution, batched GUI actions, batched GUI+CLI actions, and code execution over GUI and CLI operations. In the selected runs, code execution achieves higher task scores and fewer steps than each alternative across all three models (Figure <a href="#S3.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 3.3.2 CUA versus GCUA ‣ 3.3 Experiments on Agent Design ‣ 3 Agent Design: Code Execution and Harness-to-Model Decision Transfer ‣ OpenGCUA: Toward a Fully Open Stack for Generalist Computer Use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>). Relative to batched GUI actions, task scores improve by <span id="S3.SS3.SSS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">15.5 to 33.6 points</span>, while steps per task decrease by <span id="S3.SS3.SSS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">55.3% to 63.1%</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Executable control adds value beyond GUI+CLI access.</span>
The batched GUI+CLI baseline provides the same interfaces and already supports shell scripts. Nevertheless, code execution raises GLM-5.3-Flash’s task score from 55.8 to 63.2, a gain of <span id="S3.SS3.SSS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7.4 points</span>, and reduces Qwen3.8-Max’s steps per task from 66.1 to 54.9, a <span id="S3.SS3.SSS4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">17.0% reduction</span>. The key distinction is how operations are coordinated within a step. A batch fixes the sequence of GUI and shell actions in advance, whereas a program can use intermediate results to determine subsequent operations across both interfaces. Loops, conditional branches, and retries can thus consolidate work that might otherwise require multiple model calls. This unified interface also lets models apply their existing programming capabilities directly to computer interaction, rather than expressing computer interaction through a separate action-list format. Together, these properties may help explain the observed improvements in task scores and interaction efficiency.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.3.5 </span>Harness-to-Model Decision Transfer Ablation</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Most mechanisms are not designed primarily to improve task scores.</span>
We ablate the mechanisms supporting harness-to-model decision transfer and the harness-managed context policies. Using code execution as the baseline, we add each feature separately and then combine all features for Qwen3.8-Max and DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (Table <a href="#S3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 3.3.5 Harness-to-Model Decision Transfer Ablation ‣ 3.3 Experiments on Agent Design ‣ 3 Agent Design: Code Execution and Harness-to-Model Decision Transfer ‣ OpenGCUA: Toward a Fully Open Stack for Generalist Computer Use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). While <span id="S3.SS3.SSS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">todo</span> aims to support task completion, the other features primarily target observation efficiency, interpretability, or context management. We therefore assess cache reuse where relevant and check whether task scores are maintained.</p>
</div>
