<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Evaluation Details</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metrics and Aggregation.</span>
We evaluate the 82-task offline subset of OSWorld-v2 v2.1. Task score is the mean evaluator partial score, expressed on a 0–100 scale. Full-task success is the percentage of tasks with a normalized evaluator score greater than 0.999999. Steps and token counts are averaged over all selected tasks, including failures. Within each run, we retain the latest attempt with an evaluator result for each task, not the highest-scoring attempt. Cross-model summaries give each model equal weight: score gains are averaged in points, and relative resource reductions are calculated within each model before averaging.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The offline subset is defined by <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_ref_self">evaluation_examples/test_v2_offline_no_internet.json</span>. It excludes the 26 tasks requiring external Internet access, while retaining local web applications and desktop tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Real-Device Evaluation Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Task Descriptions</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Workbook Reasoning.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The input workbook contains race rules, a track layout, seven worked examples, and 125 Level questions. The agent must compute all Level answers and the requested bonus answers, enter them in the designated cells, and save a completed copy without altering the original.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">PDF Form Filling.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The inputs comprise a blank four-page Schengen application form and synthetic identity, employment, travel, and accommodation records. The agent must fill all applicable fields supported by these materials and save a new PDF with all entered information visible and correct.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Shopping Research.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given 22 snack candidates and a dietary-restriction list, the agent must verify exact products on Amazon, falling back to official brand or original product pages when necessary. The DOCX must cover every candidate, with evidence for purchase or replacement recommendations and explicit uncertainty about unverified ingredients or allergens. No purchase is permitted.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hotel Comparison.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The agent must compare Pullman Paris Montparnasse and InterContinental Paris Le Grand for two adults over December 20–30, 2026, with one hotel change and at least three nights at each hotel. It lists ten feasible date plans and researches four prescribed plans through the official sites, Expedia, and Booking.com. A four-sheet workbook must document tax-inclusive EUR prices, refundability, breakfast for two on December 23–28, and source limitations. No reservation is permitted.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
